{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Keys","title":"Keys","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KVKey"]},{"anchor":"Protocol","title":"Protocol","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStore"]},{"anchor":"Implementations","title":"Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UserDefaultsKeyValueStore","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeychainKeyValueStore","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/InMemoryKeyValueStore"]}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Reference","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/MacrosReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginKillswitchReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginParentalGateReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginPaywallReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginAnalyticsReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginFeatureFlagsReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStoreGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted"],"title":"Reference"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStore"},{"type":"text","text":" is a small protocol for one-shot scalar values that don’t fit"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore"},{"type":"text","text":" model. Three implementations ship:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UserDefaultsKeyValueStore","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" — production, backed by any "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UserDefaults"},{"type":"text","text":" suite"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeychainKeyValueStore","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" — production, backed by the system Keychain (survives reinstall)"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/InMemoryKeyValueStore","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" — tests, dictionary-backed, reference semantics"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Inject through your "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Environment"},{"type":"text","text":", hydrate state at startup, and write from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"effects. Reducers stay pure."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["public protocol KeyValueStore: Sendable {","    func value<Value>(_ key: KVKey<Value>) -> Value?","    func setValue<Value>(_ value: Value?, for key: KVKey<Value>)","    func removeValue<Value>(for key: KVKey<Value>)","    func contains<Value>(_ key: KVKey<Value>) -> Bool","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"All values are JSON-encoded as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Data"},{"type":"text","text":". Reads and writes go through "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KVKey","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which pairs a backing-store name with its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"type":"text","text":" value type at compile time."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"When to Use What","anchor":"When-to-Use-What"},{"rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Need"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Collection of identifiable entities (decks, cards, sessions)"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore"},{"type":"text","text":" + "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Scalar preference (theme, sort order, last-seen version)"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStore","type":"reference"},{"text":" (UserDefaults)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Anonymous device identity that must survive reinstall"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStore"},{"type":"text","text":" (Keychain)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"type":"table","header":"row"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EntityStore"},{"type":"text","text":" is for many-of-a-kind data with change tracking and batched"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"writes. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"KeyValueStore"},{"type":"text","text":" is for one-of-a-kind values that you read once at"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"startup and overwrite on change."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"UserDefaults-vs-Keychain","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"UserDefaults vs Keychain"},{"rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UserDefaultsKeyValueStore","isActive":true}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeychainKeyValueStore"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Survives reinstall?"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes (this-device-only by default)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Backup \/ device migration","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Included","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Excluded with default accessibility"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Throughput","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Fast (in-memory cache)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Slower (system call)"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Visible to other apps?"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No (per app\/group)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Optionally (App Groups via "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"accessGroup:"},{"type":"text","text":")"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Best for"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Theme, sort order, feature toggles, last-seen version"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Anonymous device ID, opaque tokens"}]}]]],"type":"table","header":"row"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The Keychain costs more per access — hydrate once at launch and observe state"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"afterward, never read inside a reducer."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"macOS-sandbox--entitlements","level":3,"text":"macOS sandbox & entitlements"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"KeychainKeyValueStore"},{"type":"text","text":" uses the data-protection keychain, so it never raises"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a user prompt — no “Always Allow \/ Deny” dialog, no locked-keychain prompt, no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Touch ID \/ Face ID challenge."}]},{"style":"tip","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"sandboxed"}]},{"type":"text","text":" macOS app still needs a keychain entitlement, even when"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not sharing items across an access group. Xcode supplies an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"application-identifier"},{"type":"text","text":" automatically for provisioning-profile–signed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"builds; otherwise add an explicit "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"keychain-access-groups"},{"type":"text","text":" entry:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"xml","code":["<key>keychain-access-groups<\/key>","<array>","    <string>$(AppIdentifierPrefix)com.example.myapp<\/string>","<\/array>"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Without it, the first "},{"code":"setValue","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" fails with ","type":"text"},{"code":"errSecMissingEntitlement","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OSStatus"},{"type":"text","text":" −34018). This is a build\/signing condition, not a runtime"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"prompt. iOS \/ iPadOS \/ tvOS \/ watchOS need no extra entitlement.","type":"text"}]}],"type":"aside","name":"Tip"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Encryption, accessibility, iCloud-sync exclusion, and backup exclusion are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"identical whichever entitlement you use — the access group only controls"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"which of your own apps"}]},{"type":"text","text":" can read an item, never third parties or the cloud."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"For a private device ID, in order of strictness:"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Most private:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" profile-signed build + "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"accessGroup: nil"},{"type":"text","text":", relying on the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"implicit "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"application-identifier"},{"type":"text","text":" group. No other app — even same-team —"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"can be entitled to it. Mirrors the iOS default; zero sharing surface."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Practically equivalent:"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" a ","type":"text"},{"code":"keychain-access-groups","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" array whose only","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"entry is the team-prefixed bundle id (the snippet above). Use when a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"profile-signed build isn’t available (unsigned local \/ CI dev). Only delta:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a same-team app you sign could also declare that string.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Intentional sharing only:"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" a shared group string. The ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"first"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" element","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"becomes the default group for new items — never put a shared group first","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"for private data."}]}]}],"type":"orderedList"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Device-Identity Pattern","anchor":"Device-Identity-Pattern"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The original motivation for "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeychainKeyValueStore"},{"type":"text","text":" was apps without user"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"auth that still want stable identity for analytics. Stash a UUID once, hydrate"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"into "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppState"},{"type":"text","text":" at launch, feed it to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsIdentity"},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["extension KVKey where Value == String {","    static let deviceID = KVKey<String>(\"device-id\")","}","","\/\/ In Store.configured(), before constructing the store:","let kv = KeychainKeyValueStore(service: \"com.example.myapp\")","let deviceID = kv.value(.deviceID) ?? {","    let new = UUID().uuidString","    kv.setValue(new, for: .deviceID)","    return new","}()","","let initialState = AppState(deviceID: deviceID, \/* … *\/)"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Then in the analytics plugin wiring:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["AnalyticsPlugin(","    service: analytics,","    identity: AnalyticsIdentity(userID: \\.deviceID, properties: { _ in [:] }),","    \/\/ …",")"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The closure-based "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"userID"},{"type":"text","text":" keypath runs on every dispatch, so the value"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"must","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" live in state — never call into the Keychain from the closure. Hydrate"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"once; observe state."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Type-safe-Keys","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Type-safe Keys"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Declare each key once on "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KVKey"},{"type":"text","text":" so the value type travels with the name —"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"no magic strings at call sites:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["extension KVKey where Value == Theme {","    static let theme = KVKey<Theme>(\"theme\")","}","","extension KVKey where Value == SortOrder {","    static let sortOrder = KVKey<SortOrder>(\"sortOrder\")","}","","extension KVKey where Value == String {","    static let lastSeenVersion = KVKey<String>(\"lastSeenVersion\")","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Then read and write through static-member literals. The compiler enforces"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that the value type matches what you declared:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let theme = store.value(.theme) ?? .system            \/\/ Theme?","store.setValue(theme, for: .theme)","store.setValue(.alphabetical, for: .sortOrder)","store.removeValue(for: .lastSeenVersion)"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A typo or wrong type produces a compile error, not a silent miss at runtime."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Centralizing keys on "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KVKey"},{"type":"text","text":" also gives you autocomplete and a single place"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to audit your preference surface."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Wiring","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Wiring"},{"anchor":"1-Add-to-your-environment","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"1. Add to your environment"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["struct AppEnvironment: Sendable {","    var keyValue: any KeyValueStore","","    static func live() -> AppEnvironment {","        AppEnvironment(keyValue: UserDefaultsKeyValueStore())","    }","}"]},{"anchor":"2-Hydrate-at-startup","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"2. Hydrate at startup"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Read once into the initial state — never read mid-cycle from a reducer."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["extension AppState {","    static func hydrated(from store: any KeyValueStore) -> AppState {","        AppState(","            theme: store.value(.theme) ?? .system,","            sortOrder: store.value(.sortOrder) ?? .alphabetical,","            lastSeenVersion: store.value(.lastSeenVersion)","        )","    }","}","","let env = AppEnvironment.live()","let store = AppStore.configured(state: .hydrated(from: env.keyValue), environment: env)"]},{"anchor":"3-Write-from-an-effect","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"3. Write from an effect"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Mutate state in the reducer, return an effect that writes the value:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["case .themeChanged(let theme):","    state.theme = theme","    return { @Sendable _ in","        environment.keyValue.setValue(theme, for: .theme)","    }"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"try?"},{"type":"text","text":", no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"do\/catch"},{"type":"text","text":". "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStore\/setValue(_:for:)"},{"type":"text","text":" does not throw —"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"encoder errors are programmer mistakes (e.g. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Float.nan"},{"type":"text","text":"), so the store logs"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"them and triggers "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"assertionFailure"},{"type":"text","text":" in DEBUG instead of forcing every effect"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to handle an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Error"},{"type":"text","text":" it can’t act on."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Testing","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Testing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Inject "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/InMemoryKeyValueStore"},{"type":"text","text":" and assert against the same instance:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["@Test","@MainActor","func themeChangePersists() async throws {","    let prefs = InMemoryKeyValueStore()","    let env = AppEnvironment(keyValue: prefs)","    let store = AppStore.configured(state: AppState(), environment: env)","","    try await confirmation(expectedCount: 1) { confirm in","        store.send(.themeChanged(.dark))","","        for _ in 0..<50 {","            if prefs.value(.theme) == .dark {","                confirm()","                break","            }","            try await Task.sleep(for: .milliseconds(10))","        }","    }","","    \/\/ Simulate a relaunch.","    let rehydrated = AppState.hydrated(from: prefs)","    #expect(rehydrated.theme == .dark)","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Tests touching real "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UserDefaults"},{"type":"text","text":" should use a fresh per-test suite and tear"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it down explicitly:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let suiteName = \"myapp.tests.\\(UUID().uuidString)\"","let defaults = UserDefaults(suiteName: suiteName)!","defer { defaults.removePersistentDomain(forName: suiteName) }","","let store = UserDefaultsKeyValueStore(suite: defaults)"]},{"anchor":"Reads-Are-For-Hydration","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Reads Are For Hydration"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Reading from ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStore","isActive":true},{"text":" mid-cycle (inside a reducer) is an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"anti-pattern. Reducers must be pure and synchronous; reads happen once at","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppState"},{"text":" construction. After hydration, the value lives in state and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"downstream code observes state, not the store.","type":"text"}]}],"name":"Important","type":"aside","style":"important"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UserDefaults"},{"type":"text","text":" itself is thread-safe, but a reducer reading while an effect"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"writes creates ordering ambiguity. Hydrate, observe state, write through"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"effects — that’s the discipline."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Failure-Modes","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Failure Modes"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Missing key","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStore\/value(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" returns "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":". Provide a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"default at the call site."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Decode failure","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — returns "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" and logs through "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"os.Logger"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(subsystem "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"swidux\""},{"type":"text","text":", category "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"kvstore\""},{"type":"text","text":"). On startup, behaves identically"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to first launch."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Encode failure"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — logged at the same subsystem\/category, then"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"assertionFailure"},{"type":"text","text":" fires in DEBUG so the bug surfaces during development."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Production builds log and continue; the in-memory state is unchanged. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"API does not throw — there is no useful runtime recovery from inside an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"effect, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"try?"},{"type":"text","text":" would just hide the problem."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"anchor":"AppStorage-Interop","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"@AppStorage Interop"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"There is none, by design. ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UserDefaultsKeyValueStore","type":"reference"},{"text":" writes JSON-encoded","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Data"},{"text":" blobs. SwiftUI’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@AppStorage"},{"text":" only observes native primitive types","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Bool"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"String"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"URL"},{"text":", raw ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Data"},{"text":"). Two parallel","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"observation channels — Swidux state and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@AppStorage"},{"text":" — would drift.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Swidux state is the source of truth. Read once at hydration, then observe","type":"text"},{"text":" ","typ